<section class="page-section" style="max-width:760px;">

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:2em;">
    <h2 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Tui Farms is a family farm in Manheim, in the heart of Lancaster County.
      We raise cattle and grow seasonal produce on the same ground our family
      works every day, and we sell what we raise directly to neighbors — no
      middleman, no mystery about where your food comes from.
    </p>
    <%# OWNER: confirm/replace — add your family's own story here (how long
        you've farmed, who's involved, anything you'd tell a visitor). %>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:2em;">
    <h2 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">How we farm</h2>
    <p>
      Our cattle are pasture-raised and responsibly finished right here on the
      farm. In produce season, sweet corn is picked fresh from the field — we
      pick what we sell, so text ahead and we'll tell you what's at its best
      today. Strawberries follow the same rule each May and June: picked ripe,
      sold fresh.
    </p>
    <%# OWNER: confirm/replace — add specifics you're comfortable stating
        (feed, pasture rotation, sprays or lack thereof, etc.). %>
  </div>

  <div class="card" id="dairy-beef" style="margin-bottom:2em;">
    <h2 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">Beef vs. dairy-beef — what's the difference?</h2>
    <p>
      We sell both, and the honest answer is: less than you'd think.
      <strong>Dairy-beef</strong> means steers that come from our dairy herd,
      raised with the same care and the same pastures as our beef cattle.
      The marbling is a little different, and it's an excellent value —
      many customers can't tell the difference at the dinner table.
      If you're not sure which cut or type to try, just ask when you text.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:2em;">
    <h2 style="color:var(--primary); margin-top:0;">How buying works</h2>
    <p>
      There's no online cart here — you text <strong>717-803-1649</strong> and a
      real person answers. Tell us what you'd like, and we'll confirm
      availability and total cost, then arrange farm pickup at
      2778 Spooky Nook Rd or delivery ($2.50/mile to your door).
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="/contact">How to order</a>
  </div>

  <p class="dairy-teaser">
    Coming in the future: Tui Farms Dairy — milk bottled right here on the farm.
  </p>
